These are the quick installation instructions for those, who like me 
can't be bothered to read the full manual.

Extract the contents of GPLOTA.ZIP into the current directory, and 
start MCLINK with the 3-Link connected and Link switched on.  Using the 
S3a copy INSTALL.OPO to any \OPO directory (The internal drive is 
advised as this file is only needed for quick installation)

Launch Install from under the OPO icon on the system screen, you will be 
asked for the drive you are installing from (the PC drive, REM::) and 
the drive to install to (LOC::).  Install will then copy the relevant 
files to the appropriate directories (these will be created if they 
don't exist)  All going well there will be no errors reported and you 
can proceed to install the icon on the system screen, with Psion+I and if
you wish assign a hot key to the Icon, with Psion+A.

